From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] taskschd: Data, the registration's security descriptor, XmlText parts, For Each

What was still E_NOTIMPL in the task definition's object model:

- ITaskDefinition::Data is kept and written as the task's <Data> element
  (and read back), for programs that keep their own data with a task.
- IRegistrationInfo::SecurityDescriptor is kept (VT_BSTR, VT_EMPTY when
  none) and written and read as <SecurityDescriptor>.
- XmlText of IRegistrationInfo, ITaskSettings and IActionCollection: the
  part as the whole task writes it; set from a fragment whose root is that
  element (the actions through a definition of their own, then copied).
- IActionCollection and ITriggerCollection _NewEnum: an IEnumVARIANT of
  the items as VT_DISPATCH; and the collections' Item and _NewEnum carry
  the standard dispids (DISPID_VALUE, DISPID_NEWENUM, as in the SDK's IDL)
  so that For Each / Enumerator in scripts reach them.

Wine's taskschd tests: the todo_wine on get_SecurityDescriptor removed; no
failures.

Gate: test/taskxml-gate.sh (test/taskxml.js under cscript, 64- and
32-bit). Mutant SG_MUTANT_NO_TASK_DATA (taskschd/task.c).
---
